# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the root of the build output. It lives in
# public/ because that is the one directory Vite copies verbatim — anything else
# would be treated as a module and bundled away.
#
# This is the same policy as the <meta> tag in index.html, plus the two parts a
# <meta> tag cannot carry: frame-ancestors, and every header that is not a CSP.
# Once this is live the <meta> tag comes out, so there is one policy rather than
# two that drift.
#
# No _redirects file is needed: routing is fragment-based, so every URL is
# index.html already and there is no path for the server to rewrite.
#
# HSTS carries no `preload`, deliberately. Preloading is a submission to a list
# compiled into browsers, slow to enter and slower to leave, and it is not ours
# to make: pages.dev is on the Public Suffix List, so the promise would be about
# a hostname Cloudflare owns. includeSubDomains is safe here — the only
# subdomains are Pages' own preview deployments, HTTPS already.
#
# connect-src names four hosts (v0.5): the barcode lookup on musicbrainz.org,
# and the cover that follows it — coverartarchive.org answers with a redirect to
# archive.org, which redirects again to one of its *.archive.org mirrors, and a
# fetch has to be allowed at every hop. It is the line that makes "nothing else
# leaves" enforced rather than stated. camera is (self) for the live scanner — a
# file input never needed it; getUserMedia does.
#
# connect-src also allows 'self' (v0.6), for the service worker. A worker runs
# under the CSP of its own script response — this same /* rule — and caching
# the app is a same-origin fetch. A looser policy for /sw.js alone is not
# possible here: Pages joins two values of one header with a comma, which
# enforces both. 'self' reaches only Spindle's own static files, and nothing
# there receives or stores data.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://musicbrainz.org https://coverartarchive.org https://archive.org https://*.archive.org; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
